(6825438, 106, 83080, '<td valign="top">This shot deserves a comment every year or so doesn''t it?  Great DOF!  <br/> <br/>Regarding the score discussion, consider this shot in the context of the other entries in this challenge (and the fact that it was shot in 2002) and it is clearly the outstanding shot, by a huge margin, in this challenge, the score makes sense to me.  The difference between #1 &amp; #2 doesn''t get much more stark.<br/> <br/>Putting it in the context of pictures regularly gracing the front page of this site in more recent years years, this shot &amp; its score are a testament to how wildly successful DPC has been in promoting great photography and photo education.<br/> <br/>A decade+ after the fact, I''d like to say congratulations Langdon on the Table Shot challenge &amp; thanks for the site.</td>', 'This shot deserves a comment every year or so doesn''t it?  Great DOF!   Regarding the score discussion, consider this shot in the context of the other entries in this challenge (and the fact that it was shot in 2002) and it is clearly the outstanding shot, by a huge margin, in this challenge, the score makes sense to me.  The difference between #1 & #2 doesn''t get much more stark. Putting it in the context of pictures regularly gracing the front page of this site in more recent years years, this shot & its score are a testament to how wildly successful DPC has been in promoting great photography and photo education. A decade+ after the fact, I''d like to say congratulations Langdon on the Table Shot challenge & thanks for the site.', '2012-07-23 13:58:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(6843712, 106, 91360, '<td valign="top">I have decided to stay a member in this site untill i''ll figure out what everybuddy sees and I dont..i hope it will be a long time he he</td>', 'I have decided to stay a member in this site untill i''ll figure out what everybuddy sees and I dont..i hope it will be a long time he he', '2012-08-17 13:01:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(7318727, 106, 101117, '<td valign="top">I love the fact that this photo is still the highest rated in the site. I think if that ever changed the whole place would collapse and everyone would go away and stop taking photos!<br/> <br/>This photo in a way is a testimony to how the site has evolved for good and bad. There''s not a single vote below 5, because the very worst people thought about it is, it''s reasonable, and clearly this was still an era where people voted purely on what they thought of it. That just wouldn''t happen now, even if someone submitted the perfect photo (if there is such a thing)!<br/> <br/>On the other hand, it''s not a photographic masterpiece is it? I probably wouldn''t ever come back to it if it wasn''t the top raking photo. There must be hundreds if not thousands of photos submitted over the years that are both technically and artistically better than it, but none of them have beaten it, and that is testimony to just how much the standard has increased. This is proof, if it were ever required, that people vote photos relative to the rest of the field.<br/> <br/>Well done Langdon, for not only having the top ranking photo to this day, but for giving us a site that has inspired so much skill, art, learning, debate, happiness, anger and most of all, photography!</td>', 'I love the fact that this photo is still the highest rated in the site. I think if that ever changed the whole place would collapse and everyone would go away and stop taking photos! This photo in a way is a testimony to how the site has evolved for good and bad. There''s not a single vote below 5, because the very worst people thought about it is, it''s reasonable, and clearly this was still an era where people voted purely on what they thought of it. That just wouldn''t happen now, even if someone submitted the perfect photo (if there is such a thing)! On the other hand, it''s not a photographic masterpiece is it? I probably wouldn''t ever come back to it if it wasn''t the top raking photo. There must be hundreds if not thousands of photos submitted over the years that are both technically and artistically better than it, but none of them have beaten it, and that is testimony to just how much the standard has increased. This is proof, if it were ever required, that people vote photos relative to the rest of the field. Well done Langdon, for not only having the top ranking photo to this day, but for giving us a site that has inspired so much skill, art, learning, debate, happiness, anger and most of all, photography!', '2015-02-19 17:56:25.000000', NULL, 0);
